daemon-freshports
=================

The FreshPorts freshports daemon, built and distributed as the FreeBSD
package freshports-freshports (port: FreshPorts/ports freshports-freshports).

This repository was split out of FreshPorts/daemontools, which was itself
converted from the daemontools project in the freshports-1 Subversion
repository (svn+ssh://svn.int.unixathome.org/freshports-1). README.md in
FreshPorts/daemontools describes that conversion. The split is done by
split-daemontools.sh in ~/src/freshports/git-conversion/.


Where the code lived
--------------------

The daemon has been renamed several times. This repository follows it
through each name, so its history starts on 2002-02-08:

  SVN revisions   daemontools path                     notes
  -------------   ----------------------------------   ----------------------
  r888 - r5049    trunk/freshports                     the original daemon
  r5050 - r5375   trunk/fp-daemon                      renamed in r5050
  r5376 - r5387   branches/git/fp-daemon               branch created r5376
  r5388 - r5415   branches/git/fp-freshports           renamed in r5388
  r5416 onward    branches/git/freshports              renamed in r5416

Each commit keeps only that directory, moved to the top of the repository;
commits that did not touch it are dropped. Every commit keeps its
git-svn-id: trailer, giving the original Subversion path and revision.

daemon-ingress shares this history up to r5385. In r5386 the daemon was
copied to branches/git/fp-ingress, which became the ingress daemon.
fp-daemon and ingress_svn, which remain in FreshPorts/daemontools, also
descend from it.


Branches
--------

  main          branches/git, as traced above
  FreshPorts2   the freshports directory of daemontools/branches/FreshPorts2
                (2002-2004)


Tags
----

The SVN tags form one version series under two names. The prefixes are
dropped so that each tag name is the package version, which is what a port
with USE_GITHUB expects:

  SVN tag                        git tag           created
  ----------------------------   ---------------   ------------------------
  fp-freshports-2.0.0 .. 2.0.5   2.0.0 .. 2.0.5    2020-07-18 .. 2020-07-19
  freshports-2.0.6 .. 2.0.16     2.0.6 .. 2.0.16   2020-07-19 .. 2026-03-17

Each tag is annotated with the tagger, date and message of the SVN
revision that created it, and points at the commit for the revision it was
copied from. Its tree was checked to be identical to the corresponding tag
in FreshPorts/daemontools before it was created.

2.0.0 (fp-freshports-2.0.0, created r5392) is the release as created. In
r5394 a second svn copy onto the existing tag nested a copy,
tags/fp-freshports-2.0.0/fp-freshports/, inside it; that nested copy is
not included.


Releasing
---------

Previously cut-freshports-freshports (in packaging-for-svn) tagged a
release in SVN, exported it, and copied the tarball to pkg01. With this
repository a release is a git tag named for the version; the port can
fetch it with:

  USE_GITHUB=	yes
  GH_ACCOUNT=	FreshPorts
  GH_PROJECT=	daemon-freshports


Not converted
-------------

  - svn:ignore properties; there is no .gitignore.
  - $Id$ keywords, which remain unexpanded as stored in SVN.
